    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, no failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `locality` field to the owner response, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived fields (`displayName`, `householdId`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Three files touched, each change small and cohesive:**\n\n1. **New `Locality.java` helper** \u2014 a tiny final class with a single static `of(city)` method backed by the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `UNKNOWN` for anything else. New class means zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other = 0`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` line calling `Locality.of(owner.getCity())`, mirroring the sibling derived-field mappings.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field and Jackson serializes it.\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: no existing method body was grown, the derivation lives in its own small unit, and the only edited function (`toOwnerDto`) stays at CC 1.",
